  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing for impact against tuberculosis and HIV - Belize (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Belize, TB/HIV, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Belize)This program has the following goals: To effectively detect and cure all forms of TB, MDR-TB and TB-HIV infections.  To halt the spread of HIV and HIV/TB co infections among MSM and other males at risk (sexually active men ages 19-49 years) with a focus on Belize, Stann Creek and Cayo Districts. The objectives of this program are: To improve the quality of treatment and care services to persons with HIV, TB and TB/HIV in Belize.  To increase the percentage of MSM and other males at risk (sexually active male ages 19-49 years) in BZ, SC, and CY districts who have received an HIV test and know their status</narrative>
  </description>
